560. Subarray Sum Equals K

Description:
Given an integer array nums and an integer k, find the total number of contiguous subarrays whose sum is exactly equal to k.

Test Case:

Input:  nums = [1,1,1], k = 2
Output: 2

Why?
The subarrays with sum 2 are:

[1,1]  → 2
[1,1]  → 2

So, the total number of valid subarrays is 2.

class Solution {
    public int subarraySum(int[] nums, int k) {

        // Stores the total number of subarrays
        // whose sum is equal to k
        int count = 0;

        // Choose the starting index of the subarray
        for (int i = 0; i < nums.length; i++) {

            // Reset sum for every new starting index
            int sum = 0;

            // Extend the subarray from index i onwards
            for (int j = i; j < nums.length; j++) {

                // Add the current element to the sum
                sum += nums[j];

                // If the current subarray sum is equal to k
                // then we found a valid subarray
                if (sum == k) {
                    count++;
                }
            }
        }

        // Return the total number of valid subarrays
        return count;
    }
}
